{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5}{-2+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2-4\\text{i}}{-2-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4+8\\text{i}-8\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{4+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{20}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-10-20\\text{i}}{20}=-\\frac{10}{20}-\\frac{20}{20}\\text{i}=-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ef409593a9807a67a7c665bab6dd70eacf744d33ec4cfdb2aaa25af3d1f9dc4"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-1-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}+\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-16440" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{5\\text{i}}{2+\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $2+\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $2-\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $2-\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\text{i}}{2+\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5\\text{i}}{2+\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{2-\\text{i}}{2-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{2}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\text{i}-5(-1)}{4-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\text{i}+5}{4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+10\\text{i}}{5}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+10\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{5}{5}+\\frac{10}{5}\\text{i}=1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ef409593a9807a67a7c665bab6dd70eacf744d33ec4cfdb2aaa25af3d1f9dc4"} {"question" "q-74640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "-2+\\text{i}"] ["math" "1+2\\text{i}"] ["math" "1-2\\text{i}"] ["math" "2-\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+2\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${z}_{1}=-2-7\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=6\\text{i}$, then ${z}_{1}$ divided by ${z}_{2}$ equals" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2-7\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is the imaginary number $6\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+6\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-6\\text{i},$ or simply $-6\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-6\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}_{1}}{{z}_{2}} & =\\frac{-2-7\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-7\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-6\\text{i}}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+42{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\text{i}+42(-1)}{-36(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-42+12\\text{i}}{36}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-42+12\\text{i}}{36}=-\\frac{42}{36}+\\frac{12}{36}\\text{i}=-\\frac{7}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ef409593a9807a67a7c665bab6dd70eacf744d33ec4cfdb2aaa25af3d1f9dc4"} {"question" "q-74658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{5}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{6}-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-74658" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}=($ {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-2-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-2+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-2+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-2-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-2+3\\text{i}}{-2+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+12{\\text{i}}^{2}}{(-2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\text{i}+12(-1)}{4-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12-8\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{-12-8\\text{i}}{13}=(-\\frac{12}{13})+(-\\frac{8}{13})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ef409593a9807a67a7c665bab6dd70eacf744d33ec4cfdb2aaa25af3d1f9dc4"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{12}{13}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316855" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{8}{13}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{12}{-4+3\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator is $-4+3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-4-3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4-3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{-4+3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{12}{-4+3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-4-3\\text{i}}{-4-3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(-4-3\\text{i})}{(-4)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-48-36\\text{i}}{16-(-9)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-48-36\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-48-36\\text{i}}{25}=(-\\frac{48}{25})+(-\\frac{36}{25})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/state.json" "file_sha256" "489cf813167934464cdb31aeb392d4bf3adfa80db39179c1caf48558041ef68f"} {"question" "q-316870" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14011270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1ef409593a9807a67a7c665bab6dd70eacf744d33ec4cfdb2aaa25af3d1f9dc4"} {"q